            <ArticleTitle>A randomised trial evaluating pain and bleeding after a first trimester miscarriage treated surgically or medically.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>213-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Miscarriage treated surgically and medically were compared in a randomised controlled trial evaluating pain and bleeding. Surgery is associated with less pain (P &lt; 0.03) and vaginal bleeding (duration and severity, P = 0.001) than medical treatment, fewer daily hospital attendances (2.5 compared with three, P = 0.04) but a greater drop in haemoglobin concentration (difference, 1 g/dl; CI95% = 0.3-1.6).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
